## Easy plus low rank

Easy plus low rank: $\mathbf{U} \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times r}$, $\mathbf{V} \in \mathbb{R}^{r \times n}$, $r \ll n$.
The [Woodbury](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodbury_matrix_identity) and [Sherman-Morrison](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherman%E2%80%93Morrison_formula) formulas can sometimes be used to reduce complexity:

\begin{eqnarray*}
	(\mathbf{A} + \mathbf{U} \mathbf{V}^T)^{-1} &=& \mathbf{A}^{-1} - \mathbf{A}^{-1} \mathbf{U} (\mathbf{I}_r + \mathbf{V} \mathbf{A}^{-1} \mathbf{U}^T)^{-1} \mathbf{V}^T \mathbf{A}^{-1} \\
    \text{det}(\mathbf{A} + \mathbf{U} \mathbf{V}^T) &=& \text{det}(\mathbf{A}) \text{det}(\mathbf{I}_r + \mathbf{V} \mathbf{A}^{-1} \mathbf{U}^T).
\end{eqnarray*}  

* [`WoodburyMatrices.jl`](https://github.com/timholy/WoodburyMatrices.jl) package can be useful.

